<http://tool4boxology.org/Component/node_281784888790737> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://w3id.org/beam/core#Process> .
<http://tool4boxology.org/Component/node_281784888790737> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://w3id.org/beam/core#Transform> .
<http://tool4boxology.org/Boxology/064a0c1a-f768-4453-a3d6-4a347facde4f> <http://w3id.org/beam/core#description> "The explanation system is based on RAG.\nCourse materials are indexed and later retrieved using hybrid retrieval. The LLM generates the explanations based on retrieved documents, followed by guardrails.\n\nOpen Questions:\n- Is the workflow the same for explain-on-highlight and question-answering?\n- What happens if guardrail detects issue?\n- Quality assurance of course material (content-wise and technical) as potential risk?\n" .
<http://tool4boxology.org/Annotation/064a0c1a-f768-4453-a3d6-4a347facde4f/node_1784875446231> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://w3id.org/beam/core#Note> .
<http://tool4boxology.org/Annotation/064a0c1a-f768-4453-a3d6-4a347facde4f/node_1784875446231> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Note" .
<http://tool4boxology.org/Annotation/064a0c1a-f768-4453-a3d6-4a347facde4f/node_1784875446231> <http://w3id.org/beam/core#description> "both BM25 and Maximum Marginal Retrieval (MMR)? how are they combined?" .
<http://tool4boxology.org/Boxology/064a0c1a-f768-4453-a3d6-4a347facde4f> <http://w3id.org/beam/core#note> <http://tool4boxology.org/Annotation/064a0c1a-f768-4453-a3d6-4a347facde4f/node_1784875446231> .
<http://tool4boxology.org/Boxology/064a0c1a-f768-4453-a3d6-4a347facde4f> <http://w3id.org/beam/core#context> "Dicoding is a learning platform, providing students with AI-based explanations. \nExplanations can be generated in two ways:\na) Explain-on-highlight in course material\nb) Chat-based question-answering\n\nNot depicted in diagram:\n- observability/tracing using LangFuse\n- sanitization of user message, retrieved material, course information\n- vector representation caching\n- session summarization?\n- fallback in case of unavailable model\n- unzipping course materials, file format specific pre-processing, chunking" .
<http://tool4boxology.org/Annotation/064a0c1a-f768-4453-a3d6-4a347facde4f/node_1784876272224> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://w3id.org/beam/risk#Risk> .
<http://tool4boxology.org/Annotation/064a0c1a-f768-4453-a3d6-4a347facde4f/node_1784876272224> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Risk: Potential Processing of Personal Data" .
<http://tool4boxology.org/Annotation/064a0c1a-f768-4453-a3d6-4a347facde4f/node_1784876272224> <http://w3id.org/beam/core#description> "For question-answering: question may include personal information" .
<http://tool4boxology.org/Annotation/064a0c1a-f768-4453-a3d6-4a347facde4f/node_1784876575107> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://w3id.org/beam/core#Note> .
<http://tool4boxology.org/Annotation/064a0c1a-f768-4453-a3d6-4a347facde4f/node_1784876575107> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Note" .
<http://tool4boxology.org/Annotation/064a0c1a-f768-4453-a3d6-4a347facde4f/node_1784876575107> <http://w3id.org/beam/core#description> "OutputFilter? SSE? does it use AI models?" .
<http://tool4boxology.org/Boxology/064a0c1a-f768-4453-a3d6-4a347facde4f> <http://w3id.org/beam/core#note> <http://tool4boxology.org/Annotation/064a0c1a-f768-4453-a3d6-4a347facde4f/node_1784876575107> .
<http://tool4boxology.org/Annotation/064a0c1a-f768-4453-a3d6-4a347facde4f/node_1784887929387> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://w3id.org/beam/risk#Risk> .
<http://tool4boxology.org/Annotation/064a0c1a-f768-4453-a3d6-4a347facde4f/node_1784887929387> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Risk: Model/Provider Unavailable" .
<http://tool4boxology.org/Annotation/064a0c1a-f768-4453-a3d6-4a347facde4f/node_1784887929387> <http://w3id.org/beam/core#description> "The model or provider preferred by the user is not available at runtime." .
<http://tool4boxology.org/Annotation/064a0c1a-f768-4453-a3d6-4a347facde4f/node_1784888000354> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://w3id.org/beam/risk#RiskControl> .
<http://tool4boxology.org/Annotation/064a0c1a-f768-4453-a3d6-4a347facde4f/node_1784888000354> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Risk Control: Fallback to Different Model" .
<http://tool4boxology.org/Annotation/064a0c1a-f768-4453-a3d6-4a347facde4f/node_1784888000354> <http://w3id.org/beam/core#description> "In case a model/provider is unavailable, fallback to using a different one at inference time." .
<http://tool4boxology.org/Annotation/064a0c1a-f768-4453-a3d6-4a347facde4f/node_1784888288944> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://w3id.org/beam/core#Note> .
<http://tool4boxology.org/Annotation/064a0c1a-f768-4453-a3d6-4a347facde4f/node_1784888288944> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Note: Other Risks + Controls" .
<http://tool4boxology.org/Annotation/064a0c1a-f768-4453-a3d6-4a347facde4f/node_1784888288944> <http://w3id.org/beam/core#description> "Risks:\n- abuse/rate-limit (including shared campus IP)\n- weak API auth (non-constant-time, without lockout)\n- path traversal in memory store\n- leak raw error messages without security headers/global exception handlers\n- dependency has not been audited\n\nRisk Controls:\n- output filter fail-closed\n- rate limit\n- double fallback (factory + service level)\n- Langfuse tracing\n- schema validation\n- isolation of “explain(ation) endpoint”\n" .
<http://tool4boxology.org/Boxology/064a0c1a-f768-4453-a3d6-4a347facde4f> <http://w3id.org/beam/core#note> <http://tool4boxology.org/Annotation/064a0c1a-f768-4453-a3d6-4a347facde4f/node_1784888288944> .
<http://tool4boxology.org/Annotation/064a0c1a-f768-4453-a3d6-4a347facde4f/node_1784888384523> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <http://w3id.org/beam/risk#Risk> .
